          "id": "pg-f7742f63",
          "position": 1,
          "title": "MB REQUESTS",
          "body": "MB wants to put these 3 games into top list for review for possible math reversals\n\n- Money Train 4, Ancient Tumble, Bill and Coin 2\n\nThese games are built around several smaller progression mechanics that interact with each other. They're all high-volatility titles (Bill & Coin 2 is medium-high), have a 96.10% RTP, and average around 4.2/5 player ratings across casino websites. It seems this layered progression approach is well received by players and keeps the gameplay engaging.\n\nIntel is coming from a marketing directors resume listing top performing games.\n-- from @Anna via @Greg\n\n---\nRoulette Game\n\n[link to example of game](https://www.youtube.com/shorts/ID56aok-s20) assigned to @joshua -t 7/31\n\n**NEED SOFT SPEC**\nMATH needed for the multiplier adds\nART grumpy Vlad for 3d renders + quality team member\n\n---\nfortune gems 500\n\n---\n# NEED 3 POTS HERC - END OF MONDAY\n# NEED (SHERWOOD heist II) THEIVES - END OF MONDAY",
          "updated": 1785521605,
          "mark": "hot"
        },
